bound-lock/1 about="Clone, `{check}`. A case that gives you a different answer is the contribution: send it with what it printed.\n{open} conjectures are open, each in the README under Open, and each says what would close it and who could.\nNothing else is asked. Lines land through the fold, never by hand; a page and the lock disagree, the lock is right." at=witness:a-parenthesis-in-the-guide by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contributing sig="ed25519:era1:R22xipMSg3X+E8OPm5wAmGlAreQ6UeA1qZqQtwCt12UZjpcd055ILDG8l/qlXM5gJUstSW3g7MPEFJukRZ8SDA==" value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Every quantity a system answers for has two marks on one scale. The floor is what must hold, the ceiling is what may hold, and the pair is a cell. Two origins that touch one cell and whose marks meet make information; two whose marks do not meet make a fork that no average can close.\n\nFour words carry the whole library. A floor, a ceiling, an origin and an epoch. A price is the distance between the marks, a state is where they stand, a verdict is what an origin found, a horizon is what no origin has reached, and none of them is a new idea: each is read off those four." at=policy:prose/idea by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/idea sig="ed25519:era1:aFDmq6crIY/LhPB85PPa32ka/iP0IR8Dn0uqC2n0kXNOxZAntpelO26IGOr58Uk0fTpfZcRvWnvolxyPwP23Cg==" value=present
bound-lock/1 about="A cell is drawn as bars on one scale: a grey bar is what one origin claims, potential until another meets it, and a green bar is where two claims meet, its ends the floor and the ceiling. A state carries its render in a figure, a badge and a graph alike: FREE green, REQUIRED grey, FORBIDDEN red, CONFLICT fork." at=policy:prose/marks by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/marks sig="ed25519:era1:wD6gqW/XkDYvXJ3FPVb+9y2NxA6zuYUHKq/pIQcRRkVMzZ5cuWc1UxWd0wvGOgsIjRLnsK75shpse2TnEohrCA==" value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="The theory here is not an application of an algebra to a problem. It is one algebra, of a cell with two marks, and three theories that turn out to be that algebra seen from different sides: constraints with a price, states on a scale, and points with an epoch and an origin.\n\nWhat it proves is that the price of a fold, the freedom of a system in bits, the four states a verdict can hold, the spectrum a domain admits, the metric that shared observation induces and the phase an epoch carries are all consequences of the same lines. Each law names the view that implements it, and each view is a folder of the source: what is proved in the field view runs in the field view, and a law no operation reaches is a law this package refuses to claim." at=policy:prose/paper by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/paper sig="ed25519:era1:5eZji/SDkxs+tsfJsp1UMMSAwYFWulrkWHIuwSx42Z/06r0+TWqVt/BIVaYXsEz7SdZb8QAADxUw9KWVWt/kAw==" value=present
bound-lock/1 about="the algebra of a cell: two poles, origins with phase, six operations" at=policy:prose/what by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/what sig="ed25519:era1:i1XdVo9vG1tq32l5Z4EBHA9dv9pb4QMflngckgl8jdnD1wLqej5NxM7vS6vBCZtwkRhlgzxqzG8ODYjvd5srBw==" value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="the published tree's first line: its lock begins here at epoch one, judged by a bound not yet on npm; a token publishes once, and every publish after it is the trusted publisher's" at=witness:token-once-then-trusted-publisher by=owner epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=status role=writes scope=publish/bootstrap sig="ed25519:era1:pGkiUv9AHRt40TKjBEQEpsBlYIrWQfK92mZFmSeWHkSNHnkvbqI0rn+K0zKngYajP8/M9+66lMu+BEi0ol61AA==" value=obligations
